// Config/Secrets.xcconfig is now committed directly with placeholder
// values (xcodegen needs the file to exist), so you don't need to copy
// this to get started. Use this template only as a reference for the
// exact format when you fill in real values, or to reset
// Config/Secrets.xcconfig back to a clean placeholder state.
//
// Fill in your Supabase project's values before building against a real
// backend (AppEnvironment.live()). See README "Getting started" / SETUP.md.
//
// SUPABASE_ANON_KEY is the public/anon key, not the service-role key - it
// is safe to ship inside the app bundle because every table it can reach
// is protected by Row Level Security (see supabase/migrations/). Never put
// a service-role key here or anywhere in the app target (spec 7.2, 14.1).
//
// Xcode build settings can't contain "//" or certain punctuation, so the
// Supabase URL/key are written without a scheme-breaking value here; keep
// them on one line each with no trailing comment.
SUPABASE_URL = https:/$()/your-project.supabase.co
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = your-anon-key-here
